  "customizablearea_parsys": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
    "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Tue May 20 2025 13:51:41 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue May 20 2025 13:51:41 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_copy": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "bottomPadding": "2",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Fri Oct 25 2024 18:38:29 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<p>Stroke is a leading cause of death and disability worldwide.<sup>1</sup> For survivors, life after a stroke is a unique and often challenging journey. In Merryl's case, he dismissed early warning signs for nearly two days, mistakenly believing his symptoms would resolve on their own. As a survivor, he is passionate about raising awareness of the critical importance of seeking immediate medical attention after experiencing any stroke symptoms to minimize potential damage and disability.</p>\n<p>“As I go back and look at it, I had all of the symptoms of a stroke, except for one, and I chose to ignore it,” said Merryl. “<b>B.E. F.A.S.T.</b> is an acronym used for the symptoms of a stroke. B stands for loss of balance. E stands for drooping eyes or blurred vision. F stands for face - a drooping face. A stands for weakness of your arms. S stands for speech, slurred speech, and T stands for time to get medical attention as quickly as possible.”</p>\n<p>Thanks to his wife for getting him to the hospital and the skilled intervention of local healthcare professionals, Merryl received treatment for the blood clot in his brain.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue May 20 2025 14:21:44 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "bottomPadding": "2",
          "jcr:createdBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "leftPadding": "3",
          "topPadding": "3",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Tue May 20 2025 13:54:29 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\">Reflecting on his experience, Merryl emphasizes, </span></span><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-2-5em\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">“</span></span></span></span><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\">I am an example to my entire family that you don't let setbacks define you.</span><span class=\"fontsize-2-5em\">”</span><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"fontsize-2em\"><br>\n </span></span></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue May 20 2025 15:11:34 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "rightPadding": "3",
          "backgroundColor": "rgb(237,238,236)",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text_1346948280": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "topPadding": "2",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Tue May 20 2025 13:56:32 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<p>Since his stroke, Merryl has been remarkably active. He's built a storage shed in his backyard, constructed a pavilion for outdoor gatherings, and begun renovating his basement. He has also returned to work full-time. Merryl is moving forward, enjoying an active lifestyle and cherishing time with his loved ones.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue May 20 2025 13:58:47 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text_1424914312": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "topPadding": "2",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Tue May 20 2025 14:08:10 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-8em\">Life after a stroke – Merryl’s stroke survivor story</span></span></h2>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue May 20 2025 14:10:25 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
